{"schema_version":"benchmark-q1-semantic-issue-coverage-judgment-luna5","question_id":"Q1-semantic-issue-coverage","status":"ok","judge_run_name":"luna8-v4-medium-196-kimi-k3-max-full200-2026-09-29","prediction_set_name":"kimi-k3-max-full200-2026-09-29","paper_id":"2504.04069","judge_input_sha256":"76b7b0823ceff088159055751f4a82704f9cedfc3156f799da2837597e8796f2","gold_decisions":[{"gold_issue_id":"2504.04069:I001","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-004","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2504.04069:I001:U001","2504.04069:I001:U002","2504.04069:I001:U005"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-004:U001","ISSUE-004:U002","ISSUE-004:U005"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue concerns the absence of a rational, polynomial-bit encoding and construction bound for a reduction using spectral normalization and a Cholesky factor. ISSUE-004 concerns an inverted variable substitution in a separate circulant-cone lemma; its scaling repair does not recognize the discrete encoding or complexity obligation.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2504.04069:I002","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-002","focus_relation":"different_obligation_or_hypothesis","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2504.04069:I002:U001","2504.04069:I002:U002","2504.04069:I002:U009"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-002:U001","ISSUE-002:U002","ISSUE-002:U007"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is a missing nonpositive-objective condition in the implication from local minimum to Nash pair. ISSUE-002 concerns a separate characterization of the boundary case lambda*=||A|| and missing single-ray/alignment conditions, not local-versus-blockwise optimality.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2504.04069:I003","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-004","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2504.04069:I003:U001","2504.04069:I003:U003","2504.04069:I003:U007"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-004:U001","ISSUE-004:U005"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is that an arbitrary scaled basis is incorrectly treated as producing the orthogonal projector VV^T, invalidating the nonnegative-eigenvector feasibility test and BFAS branch. ISSUE-004 is an unrelated scaling inversion in a circulant lemma and does not diagnose the projector/basis-normalization defect.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2504.04069:I004","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-004","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2504.04069:I004:U001","2504.04069:I004:U003","2504.04069:I004:U007"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-004:U001","ISSUE-004:U005"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue concerns the spectral-radius/compressed-norm identity under non-orthonormal image bases U_G and U_H. ISSUE-004 concerns an inverted substitution and recovery formulas in a different lemma; it does not identify the basis-normalization error in the spectral identity.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2504.04069:I005","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-003","focus_relation":"no_substantive_overlap","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2504.04069:I005:U001","2504.04069:I005:U003","2504.04069:I005:U007"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-003:U001","ISSUE-003:U002","ISSUE-003:U006"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is the false convexity premise caused by sphere-constrained block updates and the resulting unsupported AO convergence justification. ISSUE-003 concerns an undefined proposition construction when rho(A_yA_x)=0, with no diagnosis of sphere nonconvexity or AO convergence.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]}],"audit":{"all_gold_ids_decided":true,"all_ranked_candidates_considered":true,"target_type_not_used_for_identity":true,"severity_not_used_for_identity":true,"prediction_reuse_requires_explicit_issue_support":true,"each_gold_credited_at_most_once":true,"combined_entries_are_self_contained_diagnoses":true,"support_limit_three_respected":true}}